      "narrative": "Maricopa County’s October 2026 median single-family sale price was $499,990, essentially unchanged from a year earlier.[2][8] Inventory increased to 16,708 homes, up 11.6% year over year, while supply reached 4.3 months.[2][8] Buyer activity weakened: closed sales fell 18.2% to 3,214 and pending sales dropped 46.2% to 2,147, giving buyers more negotiating leverage while sellers faced slower absorption.[2] Realtor.com data for September showed 15,780 homes for sale in the Phoenix-Maricopa market, up by 1,282 year over year, with a $499,000 median asking price, down 4.95%.[5]",
