      "narrative": "Pima County’s October 2026 median sale price was $358,460, essentially flat year over year from $358,940.[2] Inventory was elevated, with 4,645 homes on the market and more than five months of supply, while 888 closings were reported, about 17% fewer than in October 2025.[2] The combination of slower sales and expanded supply indicates greater negotiating leverage for buyers than in a tight seller’s market.[2] Mortgage rates remained a constraint, although the 30-year rate had eased to 7.11% by November 12 after reaching 7.40% earlier in October.[2]",
